\f0\b \cf0 \ul \ulc0 \strokec2 CHAPTER ONE\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \ulnone \strokec2 1. Introduction\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 The rapid growth of big data has transformed the way organizations collect, process and store customer information. Financial institutions, healthcare providers, e-commerce platforms and government agencies routinely manage millions of records through web-based services. These services are commonly implemented using REST APIs because they provide efficient communication between applications.\
Although REST APIs simplify data access, they also introduce significant cybersecurity risks. Without strong authentication, authorization and monitoring mechanisms, unauthorized users may gain access to confidential customer information. Common attacks include brute-force authentication attempts, privilege escalation, token manipulation and unauthorized data disclosure.\
This project presents the design and implementation of a secure REST API using Flask that protects access to a dataset containing 100,000 customer records. The application incorporates JWT authentication, role-based access control, password hashing using Bcrypt, API rate limiting, activity logging and vulnerability assessment using OWASP ZAP.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

